From f2a4fb147f54adcf0f838118c1ca5a546a9165c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ozgur Guzeldereli <ozgur@guzeldereli.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 01:11:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] llama: TTF format 2 (row scale, shared-input adapter,
 expert side tensors) + PQ PLE table for qwen4exp

ttf_r: row scale after the product (scale-free trit types); ttf_ad / ttf_au: adapter on the centred input.
Expert weights [K, N, E] take [n, E] side vectors gathered by the routed ids, ttf_ad / ttf_au via mul_mat_id.
qwen4exp: per_layer_token_embd.pq_cb (codebooks) + pq_blob (keep bitmap, ranks, codes; host) in place of the
dense PLE table; the host maps rows to codebook entries, the rotation is folded into ple_key / ple_value.
---
