 // A second adapter of the same form, <base>.ttf_fd / ttf_fu (+ _c / _m / _b), adds its output too: the float low-rank
 // adapter of a layer that also has a ternary one.
+//
+// Format 2 (Q38, 7 Nov 2026): <base>.ttf_r is a row scale applied after the product (before ttf_b), so W can be a
+// scale-free trit type (TQ1_P); <base>.ttf_ad [K, R] / ttf_au [R, N] is an adapter that reads the main product's
+// centred input c * x + m (ttf_au carries all its scales). For expert weights [K, N, E] every side tensor has a
+// trailing expert dimension: ttf_c / ttf_m [K, E], ttf_r / ttf_b [N, E], ttf_ad [K, R, E], ttf_au [R, N, E].
 
